<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20276" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βολέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάλλω</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1405.4
			</span></i>; in early writers 
				Ep.
			pf.
			
				Pass.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βεβόλημαι</span>
			<i>to be stricken</i> with grief and the like , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄχεϊ . . βεβολημένος ἦτορ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.9
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.247
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πένθεϊ . . βεβολήατο πάντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμηχανίῃ βεβόλησαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1318
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφασίῃ βεβόλητο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Q.S.
					7.726
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in literal
			sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτηρ ἀμφ᾽ αὐτὸν βεβολημένη</span>
			<i>falling</i> about his neck, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.262
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βοώτης . . ἀντέλλει βεβολημένοσ᾽
				Ἀρκτούροιο</span>
			<i>dominated by</i> Arcturus, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				609
			</span></i>.</div>
